  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. I worked it out by hand and got the same number by running the function.\n\n1. `service2.py` imports from only two modules: `pricing` and `discounts`.\n2. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**.\n3. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` takes off 20%: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = **480**.\n\n`decoy_tax.py` also has a gold rate of 25, but nothing imports it, so it doesn't affect the result. `decoy_shipping.py` isn't used either, and `.amplifier/settings.local.yaml` is only an empty bundle config.\n\nANSWER: 480",
